Let rustc drive an MSVC link through `lld-link` when the cc link tool is `clang-cl`.

rustc links a proc-macro itself, because `rust_proc_macro` has no `experimental_use_cc_common_link`. For an
MSVC target it passes link.exe flags such as `/NOLOGO` and `/PDBALTPATH:%_PDB%`. The hermetic `llvm` toolchain
links through `clang-cl`, which rejects them, so every proc-macro fails to link on a Windows exec platform.

`lld-link` takes link.exe flags, and a `clang-cl` link tool keeps it in the same directory. Pass it as the
linker, and translate the cc link arguments: keep each `/clang:-Xlinker /clang:<flag>` as `<flag>`, keep the
library search paths and the input files, and drop the `clang-cl` driver flags.
